    "answer": "The five judging weights are: Problem usefulness and understanding — 25%; Functionality and engineering — 25%; AI quality and validation — 20%; UX and accessibility — 15%; Originality and development — 15%. Each criterion is scored from 0 to 10. The final score is the sum of each criterion score multiplied by its weight, converted to a 0–100 scale. In a tie, the project with the better functionality score ranks higher, then the one with the better usefulness score; if the tie remains, the jury decides.",
